# Countering a spell removes the spell's own stack item and nothing else
# (CounterEffect.java:258, MagicStack.remove(si)). Wretched Gryff's "When you
# cast this spell, draw a card" (Mode$ SpellCast | ValidCard$ Card.Self) has
# the Gryff's card as its source, but it is an ability of its own: ai's
# Counterspell counters the Gryff and the trigger still resolves, so human
# draws the Plains. Removing every stack item sourced by the card would drop
# the trigger with the spell.
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 2 U
tapformana human 3 U
tapformana human 4 U
tapformana human 5 U
tapformana human 6 U
tapformana human 7 U
tapformana human 8 U
queue paygeneric U
queue paygeneric U
queue paygeneric U
queue paygeneric U
queue paygeneric U
queue paygeneric U
queue paygeneric U
castspell human 1
tapformana ai 30 U
tapformana ai 31 U
queue targets 1
castspell ai 32
resolvestack
